所以我们联系了詹，我们在这一集里穿插了一些非常有趣的内容。

178
00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:55.170
I asked her specifically, okay, what was it like directing your first episode?
我特意问她，好吧，执导你的第一集是什么感觉？

179
00:07:55.650 --> 00:08:01.530
And she said the thing that, like, really stressed her out the most was that she thought directors had to have all the answers.
她说最让她感到压力山大的事情，是她以为导演必须对所有问题胸有成竹。

180
00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:08.610
She was really worried that someone would ask her a question about a prop or how to set up a scene and that she wouldn't know.
她真的很担心别人会问她关于道具或者如何布置场景的问题，而她却答不上来。

181
00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:14.570
And she said someone gave her the advice to just kind of, like, fake it till you make it sort of thing.
她说有人给她的建议是，某种程度上就是“假装直到你真正掌握”。

182
00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:16.770
But Jen was like, I can't.
但詹觉得，我做不到。

183
00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:17.910
I can't fake it.
我没法装。

184
00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:21.110
If I don't know something, I'm going to shout out, I don't know.
如果我有什么不知道的，我会直接喊出来，我不知道。

185
00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:24.290
Well, Jen wears every emotion across her face, right?
好吧，詹的各种情绪都写在脸上，对吧？

186
00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:26.270
You know how Jen feels about something.
你一眼就能看出詹对某件事的感受。

187
00:08:27.510 --> 00:08:31.090
Well, I have to say, I really respect a person who says I don't know.
不过我得说，我真的很尊敬那些敢说“我不知道”的人。

188
00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:31.990
I do, too.
我也是。

189
00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:34.150
I don't need fake it till you make it.
我不需要“假装直到你真正掌握”这一套。

190
00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:36.850
I would much rather just know truly how someone's feeling.
我宁愿真切地知道别人的真实感受。

191
00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:42.630
I don't need, like, the whatever thing, the filter people put on.
我不需要那种随便什么东西，不需要人们戴上的滤镜。

192
00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:43.530
I agree.
我同意。

193
